  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1) \nHigh pressure centered over the Great Lakes will gradually shift east\nand off the coast by Tuesday. As this occurs, winds will slowly come\naround to southerly. Until then, a dry airmass will remain in place\nwith just some diurnal cumulus. Temperatures will be warming with\neach day as heights rise due to another expanding mid level high. It\nwill not get as hot as the past week, but temperatures are forecast \nto get back into the lower 90s across most of the area by Wednesday.\n\nThe building heat will also be short lived. A short wave will track\nfrom the northern Plains across the upper Great Lakes, pushing a \ncold front into the area, possibly as early as the end of Wednesday, \nbut more likely Wednesday night into Thursday. This will bring the \nnext round of showers and thunderstorms, although forecast \ninstability looks to be modest at best. Cooler, drier air will \nreturn for the end of the week.",
